{"id":"s4","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":4,"of":6,"title":"How it's done","titleHe":"תֹּאַר הַפֹּעַל","goal":"Modify a verb — with an adverb, or with a preposition and a noun.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew has fewer true adverbs than English and makes up the difference with בְּ plus an abstract noun: בְּשֶׁקֶט quietly, literally in quiet."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"הוּא מְדַבֵּר מַהֵר.","en":"He speaks quickly."},{"he":"הִיא כָּתְבָה בִּזְהִירוּת.","en":"She wrote carefully."},{"he":"אֲנִי מַכִּיר אוֹתוֹ הֵיטֵב.","en":"I know him well."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"טוֹב is an adjective doing adverb duty in speech — הוּא כּוֹתֵב טוֹב. In writing you'd want הֵיטֵב."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מַהֵר","en":"quickly","translit":"maher"},{"he":"לְאַט","en":"slowly","translit":"le'at"},{"he":"הֵיטֵב","en":"well, thoroughly","translit":"heitev"},{"he":"מְאוֹד","en":"very","translit":"me'od"},{"he":"תָּמִיד","en":"always","translit":"tamid"},{"he":"לִפְעָמִים","en":"sometimes","translit":"lif'amim"},{"he":"כְּבָר","en":"already","translit":"kvar"},{"he":"בְּשֶׁקֶט","en":"quietly","translit":"besheket"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["therefore","hello, peace","thus","quickly"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מַהֵר","translit":"maher"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["no, not","slowly","writing","football"],"correct":1,"prompt":"לְאַט","translit":"le'at"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["dog","invites, orders","well, thoroughly","under"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הֵיטֵב","translit":"heitev"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["roof","very","no, not","your (f.)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מְאוֹד","translit":"me'od"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["always","here is, behold","houses","in, at"],"correct":0,"prompt":"תָּמִיד","translit":"tamid"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["table","never","sometimes","to me"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לִפְעָמִים","translit":"lif'amim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["then","book","already","king"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כְּבָר","translit":"kvar"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["לִפְעָמִים","sometimes"],["הֵיטֵב","well, thoroughly"],["מַהֵר","quickly"],["בְּשֶׁקֶט","quietly"],["לְאַט","slowly"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “quietly”?","options":["אוּלַי","בְּשֶׁקֶט","אָנֹכִי","לוֹ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"בְּשֶׁקֶט","translit":"besheket","en":"quietly"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מְאוֹד","כְּבָר","בְּשֶׁקֶט","תָּמִיד"],"correct":0,"say":"מְאוֹד","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sometimes”?","options":["יוֹשֵׁב","לִפְעָמִים","אֵין","קוֹנֶה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “well, thoroughly”?","options":["דִּבּוּר","עֶרֶב","הֵיטֵב","בְּוַדַּאי"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “always”?","options":["עָלַי","תָּמִיד","אֶרֶץ","שָׁר"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["כְּבָר","לְאַט","מְאוֹד","בְּשֶׁקֶט"],"correct":3,"say":"בְּשֶׁקֶט","he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["תָּמִיד","מְאוֹד","הֵיטֵב","לְאַט"],"correct":3,"say":"לְאַט","he":true}]}